giants


breath breathe breathe
swallow
hear them banging in your chest
breathe breathe breathe
stay
drown them in this wet embrace
a poison seeped in
or a cure
or a curse
I'm still drowning them
these words
even in this scorching sun
as I lay here
a-sleep
a-run
a liar
a-dead

I have grown
large
so large
inside of me
that even from a breath away
I cannot see who you are
I can only...

we could have been
giants
together
we could have
grasped
at abandoned slippers..
together

if there is a giant in you
I must never know it.
to imagine it,
is violence.
and my giant?
is mine alone.
the time of sharing,
has passed.